  "result": "I fixed the option order in `--help`. Names now list short first, as in `-v, --verbose`. Before, they came out as `--verbose, -v`.\n\nThe cause was in `join_options` in `src/click/formatting.py:319`. It sorted option names by prefix length with `reverse=True`, so the longer `--` prefix came before `-`. I removed `reverse=True`.\n\nThe test suite passes (1906 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed). I didn't run the CLI to check the output by eye, and no existing test covers this ordering. If you'd like, I can add a regression test for it.",
